KG42.register("clusters-87cda7d748a3ee2637672b08",{"id":"39-dynamic_congestion_tariff::v142-d-CL001","paper":"39-dynamic_congestion_tariff","label":"DPT iterative coordination driven by aggregator demand response and DSO network verification","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL001","label":"DPT iterative coordination driven by aggregator demand response and DSO network verification","market_meaning":"In the planning stage, the DSO issues the DPT according to conventional load forecasts and network conditions; the aggregator, based on the received DPT and energy prices, forms and submits tentative demand under EV and HP operating constraints. The DSO aggregates loads, checks network limits, adjusts the signal according to residuals, and feeds it back to the aggregator for re-planning, determining the final DPT according to termination conditions.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","coordination"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"The three Rule-Chains all belong to the same DPT planning mechanism, and the functional scopes of demand formation, network verification, and signal update are complementary. Cross-chain mathematical closure still depends on consistency of the planning period, the complex load convention, and the rate representation; these conditions still have gaps. The scope of this cluster is the current EV/HP congestion coordination, and does not extend to FPT+DT, energy market clearing, or charging settlement.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The submitted demand quantity enters DSO load aggregation, the network state enters signal update, and the updated rate enters aggregator planning; these source-supported information and decision dependencies constitute the assembly boundary. The three Rule-Chains jointly express one iterative coordination candidate, each retaining its original responsibility, graph edges, and mathematical content; existing gaps mean that it cannot yet serve as a complete executable rule.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R001","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertake demand planning after receiving the DPT, EV/HP demand aggregation, and response submission; this is the participant decision end in the iteration."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R002","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertake receiving responses, combining conventional load forecasts to form network loads and checking limits; this is the network verification link connecting demand and tariff adjustment."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R003","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Undertake signal initialization, residual-driven update, non-negativity restriction, termination check, and final rate determination; this is the iterative feedback end."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x-pa-it","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g20-E20","v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22"],"rationale":"The aggregated DR formed and sent by the aggregator is the input received by the DSO and used for active power load aggregation. This mapping connects the submission end and the use end; the time-domain correspondence between N_t and N_T still needs to be verified."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"The DSO forms the current-round s_t from the conventional load and the received DR, and this load then enters the marginal signal and DPT update. Here it corresponds to the use interface of load quantity; whether the voltage expression is consistent is addressed separately in v142-d-G004."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P002","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P003","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P004","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P003","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P004","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P005","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P006","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e016"],"rationale":"The source text explicitly uses the residual generated by comparing network limits for tariff adjustment, and uses network constraint satisfaction for termination judgment. Therefore the two Rule-Chains have functional coupling; the voltage conjugate difference has not been resolved, and the two sets of frozen expressions cannot be deemed equivalent on that basis."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g16-E16","v141-b-g02-e010","v141-b-g02-e015"],"rationale":"The DSO sends the updated DPT, and the aggregator takes the received rate as a fixed input for that round's optimization, forming the subsequent DR. R001 does not yet have a local parameter object corresponding to R_t, so this is recorded as functional coupling, retaining the role distinction between the updated quantity and the received parameter."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM001","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R002::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R003::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g20-E20","v141-b-g21-E21"],"rationale":"The three places reference the same existing demand submission node, and respectively relate to the formation, reception, and feedback use of demand in the same DPT iteration. The representative reference is for display only, and each original reference and binding is retained."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM002","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g02-e015"],"rationale":"Both places reference the DPT coordination node used for aggregator re-planning. The reference in the signal update Rule-Chain is selected as the display representative, retaining the local bindings at the update end and the response end."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM003","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::x-pa-it","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g20-E20","v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22"],"rationale":"The source text directly identifies the aggregated DR formed by Equation (6) as the quantity received by the DSO and used for load aggregation, supporting the semantic correspondence between the submission end and the reception end. The two local objects are retained; their time-period set difference is addressed in v142-d-G003."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM004","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e010"],"rationale":"Both are the bus total apparent load obtained by the DSO from conventional load and aggregated DR; R003 further has an iterative use role. Retain their respective indices, domains, and bindings; this same-quantity correspondence does not eliminate the conjugate difference in the voltage expression."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM005","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P001","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P003"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"The vocabulary and update description point the two D occurrences to the PTDF in the same mechanism, used respectively for line verification and for residual and rate transformation. The two local uses remain independent, and the matrix dimension still needs to be verified."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM006","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P004"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Both F_t occurrences correspond to the same line active power load limit, serving respectively as the verification bound and the reference quantity for the update residual. Retain the local expressions of the line and time-period indices."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM007","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P003","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P005"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g23-E23","v141-b-g02-e018","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Both Z occurrences are defined by the inverse of the same partial node admittance matrix, serving respectively voltage verification and signal transformation. Parameter identity correspondence does not mean that the voltage expressions in which they occur are already consistent."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM008","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P004","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P006"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"Both V_0 occurrences are defined by the vocabulary as the voltage at node 0, and are used for normalization in the same network voltage verification and update. Retain the local parameter objects of the two Rule-Chains."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-OM009","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P005","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P007"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011"],"rationale":"The existing definitions of both objects refer to the voltage lower limit, and the source text explains the update term as the residual of the corresponding voltage constraint, supporting a tentative same-quantity correspondence. The underline marking difference in the quotation is retained in v142-d-G004, and no representative is selected or expression merged."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"The B entries used by this cluster remain unverified; candidate_support_evidence_ids only grants experimental candidate support eligibility. B source audit, C2 independent review, and Agent E have not been carried out, and the existing transcription and downstream scientific interpretation have not been independently confirmed.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g13-E13","v141-b-g17-E17","v141-b-g20-E20","v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011","v141-b-g02-e013"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manually check item by item the quotations, formulas, and source locations used by this cluster, and then check each assembly mapping; maintain the source status and candidate nature of this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"R001-C002 only describes the optimization process and does not provide the complete mathematical objects and bindings of Equations (1)-(5); the energy cost term in Equation (1) is transcribed inconsistently in v141-b-g02-e004 and v141-b-g17-E17. R_t is an updated quantity in R003, but a given parameter in the aggregator optimization; R001 does not yet have a corresponding local parameter object.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R001::x::x-p-it","v141-c-R001::x::x-phat-it","v141-c-R001::theta::theta-Ei","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g16-E16","v141-b-g17-E17","v141-b-g18-E18","v141-b-g19-E19","v141-b-g02-e004","v141-b-g02-e005"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify Equation (1) and confirm the scope of the upstream optimization formalization, complete the typed objects and bindings required by Equations (1)-(5); clarify the parameter role of the received R_t and retain its distinction from the DSO update variable."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G003","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"Equations (2) and (6) use N_t, while the vocabulary and other related formulas use N_T; the existing material does not explain whether the two sets are the same. The submission and reception of aggregated DR can be semantically corresponded, but their complete time domains cannot yet be directly equated.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::x::x-pa-it","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X001","v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-P009","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g18-E18","v141-b-g20-E20","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e011"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the original definition of the time-period set, confirm whether it is a notational difference or a different applicable domain, and then have upstream clarify the cross-chain index correspondence."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G004","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The voltage check in R002-C002 uses the conjugate of s_t, while the voltage residual in R003-C004/C007 does not use the conjugate; the underline marking of the voltage lower limit in the corresponding B quotation is also inconsistent. Under the existing complex load definition, the two cannot be directly deemed to express the same limit condition.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-X002","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X004"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e007","v141-b-g02-e009","v141-b-g02-e011"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify Equations (8) and (12), the complex power sign convention, and the voltage lower-limit notation, and have upstream explain or revise the difference; before that, retain the two sets of frozen expressions and their undetermined relationship."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G005","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The domain of R003-X003 is an N_d×N_d matrix, but according to the existing uses of PTDF, load, and marginal signal, the right-hand side of the rate transformation in R003-C007 appears as a bus vector; its representation relationship with the R_t matrix used in the aggregator quadratic form is not clear.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X003","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P003","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E02","v141-b-g04-E04","v141-b-g16-E16","v141-b-g17-E17","v141-b-g02-e011"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify Equation (13) and the vector and matrix conventions of R_t, and have upstream clarify the dimensions of each object and the source-supported representation conversion, completing the dimensional interface from the rate to the aggregator objective."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G006","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The source text supports first clipping the marginal signal, then transforming the rate, and using the modified signal to check convergence; the frozen formulas express these contents separately. C004 also does not explain the comparison convention for the absolute value of a vector or matrix, and the implementation order and numerical stopping criterion still need explicit alignment.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C004","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C005","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e012","v141-b-g02-e013","v141-b-g02-e016"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Have upstream clarify the applicable order among the clipping with iteration label, the rate transformation, and the stopping check, and verify whether the absolute value comparison is component-wise or uses a specific norm."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G007","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The control explanation in III-B requires readjustment of the voltage signal, but the current Rule-Chain does not include this coefficient or its application position. Therefore this cluster only covers the existing basic iteration expression and does not yet cover a control implementation including readjustment.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C007","v141-c-R003::x::v141-c-R003-X002","v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-P001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e017","v141-b-g02-e021"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Confirm the applicable scope of the readjustment version; if this implementation needs to be covered, have upstream specify the readjustment position, conditions, and typed parameters, and distinguish the general mechanism from the case configuration."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G008","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The source text requires the aggregator to keep its energy consumption level within the capacity revealed by the final round of DR; the three chains record DR submission and final DPT determination, but do not establish corresponding commitment or execution clauses or the capacity basis. The determination of the final tariff has not yet formed a complete energy-use obligation chain.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::x::x-pa-it","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g14-E14","v141-b-g02-e003"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should supplement the responsible entity for the final-round DR capacity commitment, the applicable time period, the meaning of capacity and its relationship with the final tariff, and clarify whether it falls within the scope of subsequent execution."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-G009","category":"ontology_extension","description":"The six node proposals involving the power-based network tariff, demand aggregators and DSO network verification remain pending. Existing generic nodes only provide the current binding; therefore DPT cannot be interpreted as a transaction clearing price, nor can DSO network verification be interpreted as market clearing.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R001","v141-c-R002","v141-c-R003"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R001::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R001::V::coordination.price_signal","v141-c-R002::V::coordination.local_operator","v141-c-R003::V::coordination.price_signal"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g12-E12","v141-b-g15-E15","v141-b-g21-E21","v141-b-g22-E22","v141-b-g02-e014"],"proposal_ids":["proposal:pricing.power_tariff","proposal:participation.aggregator","proposal:validation.network_limit_check","proposal:v141-b-g02-dpt","proposal:v141-b-g02-aggregator","proposal:v141-b-g02-dso"],"required_work":"Manually assess the six proposals and their semantic overlap item by item, and clarify the applicable framework mapping; this round continues to retain the unapproved status of the existing graph objects and proposals."}]},"rule_refs":["39-dynamic_congestion_tariff::v141-c-R001","39-dynamic_congestion_tariff::v141-c-R002","39-dynamic_congestion_tariff::v141-c-R003"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-054a3024f5d3e00d","COMP-181ce7e5da973b5d","COMP-221ff4096aa50456"]});
